{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of task #5525: `[stitch] Implement cmd/link core functionality (srd084-link R1.1-R1.4)`. This requires creating two files:\n   - `cmd/link/main.go` - A Go utility that creates hard links using the `link(2)` system call\n   - `cmd/link/link_test.go` - Differential tests comparing output against the GNU reference binary `glink`\n   \n   The task requires implementing: hard link creation from two arguments using link(2), proper exit codes (0 on success, 1 on error), `--help` flag, `--version` flag, SIGPIPE handling, and proper error messages for wrong argument counts and failed link(2) calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `link(2)` system call for creating hard links (Go: `syscall.Link`)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing against Homebrew GNU `glink`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Manual argument parsing (no cobra framework for simple utilities)\n   - Binary name normalization in tests for stderr comparison\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"glink\")` with `t.Skip` pattern for graceful skip when reference binary absent\n   - Custom test helper functions for file-state verification tests (link creation verification)\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd084-link.yaml` (read)\n     - Defines the SRD for cmd/link with two requirement groups: R1 (hard link creation) and R2 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - R1.1: Accept exactly two args, create hard link using link(2)\n     - R1.2: Must not follow symlinks, create symlinks, or handle directories specially\n     - R1.3: Exit 1 with error to stderr if wrong number of arguments\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 with error to stderr if link(2) fails\n     - R2.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R2.2: Exit 1 on any error\n     - R2.3: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully using `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n     - Non-goals: no symbolic links, no multiple targets, no directory handling\n\n   - `cmd/unlink/main.go` (read - reference pattern for similar utility)\n     - Key pattern to follow for cmd/link:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: unlink FILE\n       or:  unlink OPTION\n     Call the unlink function to remove the specified FILE.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `unlink (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             switch arg {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n         }\n         if len(args) == 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: missing operand\\n\")\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if len(args) > 1 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[1])\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if err := syscall.Unlink(args[0]); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: cannot unlink '%s': %s\\n\", args[0], capitalizeErr(err))\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func capitalizeErr(err error) string {\n         msg := err.Error()\n         if len(msg) > 0 {\n             return strings.ToUpper(msg[:1]) + msg[1:]\n         }\n         return msg\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/unlink/unlink_test.go` (read - reference pattern for differential tests)\n     - Key patterns: binary name regex normalization, `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `exec.LookPath(\"gunlink\")`, `discardStdout` normalizer for --help/--version, custom `runRemovalTest`/`runBin`/`compareResults` helpers for file-state tests, `context.WithTimeout` for binary execution\n     - Full file content captured above (190 lines)\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided in prompt context)\n     - Exports `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` which sets up SIGPIPE signal notification and exits 0 on receipt\n\n   - `cmd/link/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n   - `cmd/link/link_test.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified the reference patterns from `cmd/unlink` for both implementation and testing\n   - Noted that `link` needs exactly 2 arguments (vs unlink's 1), requiring adjusted argument validation\n   - Noted that link creates files (vs unlink which removes), so tests need to verify hard link creation (inode matching) rather than file removal\n   - The GNU error format for link is `link: cannot create link 'FILE2' to 'FILE1': Error message` based on GNU coreutils conventions\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task specification with full project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, requirements, constraints, and instructions to implement cmd/link (srd084-link R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT ca